T-BOYS DUO CIRCUIT — JMLOGIC DELTA v0.1.2

DAMAGE OWNERSHIP
- During an ordinary committed action, damage ownership stays with the team whose turn/action is live.
- The attacker does not take hidden recoil or self-damage merely because post-collision velocity becomes lower than the recipient's velocity.
- Recoil, counter and sacrifice damage require an explicit named rule, visible warning and trace.
- One attacker may damage one defender once per committed action; repeated overlap/jitter is contact-only unless a named multi-hit route authorises more.
- Ordinary clean-hit damage is capped below full-health KO; Break Window may exceed the ordinary cap but cannot silently one-shot a full fighter.

ASSIST ROUTE GUARD
- ASSIST resolves only to a living rival.
- An allied, dead or missing requested target is rejected and replaced by the nearest valid rival.
- The partner receives a short friendly-pass window so the relay cannot home into, collide with or be redirected by its own active teammate.
- When the active teammate blocks the direct line, the assist route bends around the ally before committing toward the rival.

HANDOFF
- Single HTML first.
- Zionfolder backup second.
- Owner contact decides Ding.
